# Screen Gallery (Cursor Rule)

When the user asks to set up, update, or maintain a screen gallery / dev UI previewer:

1. Run `node .agents/skills/screen-gallery/bin/cli.mjs init` (or `--entry index` for root `/`) and `scan --write` in the frontend root (`vite.config.*` or `next.config.*`).
2. Read `SKILL.md` and `AGENTS.md` from the `screen-gallery` folder and start the dev server early for live HMR preview.
3. For rapid new pages, register `component: () => import(...)` in `src/gallery/catalog.ts` immediately with `default`, `loading`, `empty`, and `error` states.
4. Map all public & protected routes, global shells (`AppShell`), exact `/api/*` TypeScript payload shapes, and mandatory auth/session mocks (`GET /api/me` or `storage`).
5. Detect animations (`motion`, CSS keyframes, Lottie) and media (`.gif`, `.webp`, animated SVGs) and add dedicated gallery previews.
6. Use only synthetic data and `@example.test` emails. Verify with `tsc --noEmit` and `src/gallery/catalog.test.ts`.
